# README for mesa


Notes for ppc64 Mesa Overlay:

  This configuration belongs to the CRUX ppc64 overlay and provides
  a Mesa build adapted for generic 64-bit PowerPC systems (POWER4 and above).
  It enables a broad set of Gallium drivers while maintaining compatibility
  with both legacy and more modern GPUs available on ppc64 platforms.

  Vulkan, Intel-specific features, and experimental components are excluded
  by default, as they are either unsupported or unreliable across the wide
  range of ppc64 hardware (especially big-endian systems such as Power Mac G5).

  Please refer to the upstream xorg/mesa/README.md for additional context
  and general Mesa build information.


User-defined build options:

  b_lto          : false        # Disable LTO for better portability across toolchains
  b_pie          : true         # Enable PIE (default and safe on 64-bit)
  egl            : enabled      # Enable EGL for modern rendering paths
  gallium-drivers: nouveau,r300,r600,radeonsi,svga,virgl,i915,swrast
                                # Broad coverage: NVIDIA, AMD (old/new), Intel, virtualization, and software fallback
  gallium-va     : conditional  # Enabled only if libva is present
  gbm            : enabled      # Enable GBM for EGL/DRI integration
  gles1          : disabled     # Deprecated and unnecessary
  gles2          : enabled      # Required for modern lightweight applications
  glvnd          : enabled      # Vendor-neutral GL dispatch
  glx            : dri          # Use DRI-based GLX for X11
  llvm           : enabled      # Required for llvmpipe and shader compilation
  platforms      : x11[,wayland]# X11 by default; Wayland enabled if available
  shared-llvm    : enabled      # Link dynamically against system LLVM
  video-codecs   : all          # Enabled, but depends on optional runtime components
  vulkan-drivers :              # Disabled (not broadly supported on ppc64)
  vulkan-layers  :              # Disabled


Pkgfile notes:

  The Pkgfile retains a small set of conditional checks for optional
  dependencies to remain flexible while avoiding unnecessary complexity.
  Features such as VA-API, sensors, or Wayland are enabled only when the
  corresponding libraries are present.

  Vulkan support and Intel-specific features (such as ray tracing) have
  been explicitly removed, as they are not generally applicable to ppc64
  systems and may introduce build or runtime instability.

  While multiple Gallium drivers are enabled, not all of them will be
  relevant on every system. This approach ensures the package remains
  broadly usable across different ppc64 configurations without requiring
  rebuilds for specific hardware.



Summary:

  - Targets 64-bit PowerPC systems (POWER4 and above, big-endian).
  - Designed for compatibility with legacy PowerPC hardware such as G5.
  - Excludes Vulkan and Intel-specific features for stability.
  - Provides a broad set of Gallium drivers for NVIDIA, ATI/AMD, Intel, and virtual GPUs.
  - Includes software rendering fallback via llvmpipe (through LLVM).
  - Focuses on X11/DRI rendering paths with optional Wayland support.
  - Aims for a balanced Mesa build that prioritizes compatibility and maintainability.
